### 逐处错误标注
1. young people over-depend on their parents → over-dependence on parents among young people；原句两个谓语，语法冲突
2. say → says；主语 a young guy 是单数，一般现在时谓语加 s
3. love → loves；he 作主语，谓语单数
4. a excuse → an excuse；excuse 元音音素开头，用 an
5. Opinion → Opinions；后面 vary 原形，主语用复数
6. prevent → prevents；动名词短语作主语，谓语单数
7. from develop → from developing；固定搭配 prevent sb. from doing
8. Such as… 单独成句错误 → 并入前面主句，such as 不能引导独立句子
9. Once they will find → Once they enter society, they will find；once 引导状语从句，从句不用 will
10. adapt on society → adapt to society；固定搭配 adapt to（适应）
11. the sense of responsibility → a sense of responsibility；固定搭配
12. their first step → their first reaction；用词不自然，reaction 更贴合语境
13. solving it → solving them；problems 复数，代词用 them
14. In this way will they never → Otherwise, they will never；倒装误用，逻辑不对
15. get a progress → make progress；progress 不可数，固定搭配 make progress
16. living on the society → adapt to society；society 泛指社会不加 the、介词用 to
17. achieve the success → achieve success；success 表抽象成功，不加 the


### 修正版
  Nowadays, over-dependence on parents among young people has become a common phenomenon. As shown in the picture, a young guy says that he loves living with his parents, using 
it as an excuse to avoid independence. Opinions vary from person to person.
  On the one hand, over-relying on parents prevents young people from developing their vital abilities, such as solving problems and facing troubles on their own. Once they 
