###
  Nowadays, over-dependence on parents among young people has become a common phenomenon. As is shown in the picture, a young man claims that he loves living with his parents, 
using it as an excuse to avoid independence. Different people hold different views on it.
  For one thing, excessive reliance on parents prevents young people from developing essential abilities, such as solving problems and facing challenges on their own. Once they
step into society, they will find it hard to adapt. For another, this habit may make them lack a sense of responsibility. They tend to count on parents whenever troubles appear 
instead of making efforts themselves.
  From my perspective, young people should learn to be independent gradually. Only in this way can they grow into capable adults and achieve real success.
